{"id": "EUVD-2026-86851", "enisaUuid": "ad859ca6-5f12-3b04-bbfe-29c8cc6049f0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: destroy seen inode bitmap when we fail to add a dirpath\n\nLOLLM observes a memory leak in xchk_dirtree_create_path if we create\nthe directory path object but appending the name to the path fails.\nWhen this happens, we don't tear down the (empty) seen inode bitmap.\nThis is a pretty trivial error, but let's not leave logic bombs.\n\nDo the same for a similar bug in xrep_dirtree_create_adoption_path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b10ca4302ee2dda4233f70b2033883ee376fa6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b756de8167f2f06ffceadc71cb17c1fc7be4be8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/582f54dce62043f7a0503ab8c76d718d0293da59", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a441c6842da75c5b862cc1c9f7969d6a93b54b9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jm9w-mmf5-g697", "CVE-2026-97543"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "211d1c22-fbc3-3417-a486-b9f786734a3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "928b721a11789a9363d6d7c32a1f3166a79f3b5f <1a441c6842da75c5b862cc1c9f7969d6a93b54b9"}, {"id": "4058f53f-15fa-3423-aaed-92254c692fd9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "973a6a01-0f22-3004-8ba5-cb47b57b4474", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "928b721a11789a9363d6d7c32a1f3166a79f3b5f <0b756de8167f2f06ffceadc71cb17c1fc7be4be8"}, {"id": "9866c882-9a04-313f-af09-505b96727247", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "9cfb0661-ad94-3d42-a0a6-1ccd22aa761d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c7bbbc1c-9d2b-31f7-9a3b-487187829be0", "